          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the Court of Appeals for the Armed Forces previously held that military appellate courts possess open\u2011ended jurisdiction under the All Writs Act to entertain a coram nobis challenge to the merits of a final court\u2011martial conviction."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dfee6d22d9f1f5e78b067ccae1581c7d525e8182b53deb9937581ec94685df13",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dfee6d22d9f1-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked how the issue differs from the general rule that a judgment becomes final and has preclusive effect once the appellate route has been exhausted or the time to pursue it has expired."
      }
    ],
