              "document_hash": "dfee6d22d9f1f5e78b067ccae1581c7d525e8182b53deb9937581ec94685df13",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-dfee6d22d9f1-0000-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 16,
                "start": 16
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, military appellate courts lack jurisdiction under the All Writs Act because Congress did not confer such authority."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "dfee6d22d9f1f5e78b067ccae1581c7d525e8182b53deb9937581ec94685df13",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-dfee6d22d9f1-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the Uniform Code of Military Justice limits appellate jurisdiction to the findings and sentences of a court\u2011martial; it does not permit further review such as coram nobis."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "dfee6d22d9f1f5e78b067ccae1581c7d525e8182b53deb9937581ec94685df13",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-dfee6d22d9f1-0000-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 16,
                "start": 16
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, congress could legislate broadly for collateral remedies, but the All Writs Act does not itself provide an independent basis of jurisdiction; such basis exists only in Article\u202fIII courts."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Shah (Petitioner)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "dfee6d22d9f1f5e78b067ccae1581c7d525e8182b53deb9937581ec94685df13",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-dfee6d22d9f1-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 56,
                "start": 56
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Shah (Petitioner), according to Mr. Shah (Petitioner), the government\u2019s position is that a person who has completed his enlistment cannot be retried in military courts after a conviction is set aside."
        }
      ],
